  (:id "keys-and-backends-planned"
   :title "Keys and backends"
   :text "What a game team needs to run its own connect-token backend: its own keypairs, the guide in KEYS.md, and the example backends in Go and C# under examples/backend. The keypair, guide and backend files are in the tree; their rows stay not-done until a recorded run qualifies them."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Key generator: a rocketnet_keygen tool, built with the SDK, writing a fresh Ed25519 signing keypair and the token encryption key for production" :cells (n n n) :note "the server takes the public key; the private key stays on the backend; it replaces the published development keys. References: netcode's keygen and yojimbo's (keygen.cpp at the repository root is the starting point)")
    (:feature "Keys documentation: a KEYS.md guide to generating keypairs, where each key lives, rotation, and rocketnet_write_production_connect_token" :cells (n - -) :note "a document. Covers where each key lives (backend, server, and never shipped in the client), rotation, and development keys versus production keys. References: netcode's and yojimbo's key documentation")
    (:feature "Example backends in Go and C#: a minimal HTTP backend in each that authenticates a player (stub), mints a connect token with the production keys for a chosen server address, and returns it for rocketnet_client_connect" :cells (n n n) :note "each comes with a connect token format test vector shared with the C SDK, so tokens minted in Go and C# are accepted by the server. References: the netcode connect token and the yojimbo matcher backend (Go). Restated 2026-10-21: backends in Go and C# that mint connect tokens, like yojimbo's matcher; landed with PR #430 (28e0d7d5)")
    (:feature "Client example: fetches a connect token from the example backend and connects with it" :cells (n n n) :note "the Go and C# example backends under examples/backend mint connect tokens; a client example that fetches a token from one of them and connects with it is not qualified by a recorded run at this head")))
  (:id "correctness-post-v1"
   :title "Correctness after v1.0.0-preview-1 (later)"
   :text "Correctness work that follows v1.0.0-preview-1."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "TLA+ invariants NoReceiveUnlessRunning and NoAdmitUnlessRunning on the server lifecycle, plus tests that a stopping or stopped server reads no packet and admits no client" :cells (n n n) :note "the query itself ships as rocketnet_server_running in v1.0.0-preview-1")))
  (:id "preview-2-known-issues"
   :title "Preview-2 known issues (carried into preview-3 where still open)"
   :text "Current limits accepted for the preview-2 cut. These rows describe preview-2; the historical preview-1 table below is retained only as history."
   :label "known issue"
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "AF_XDP copy mode with one Windows portable client passed through 500 clients, but the 1000-client start failed after eight server connections hit reliable timeouts. The same Windows client passed 1000 clients against the portable Linux server." :cells (n - n))
    (:feature "The macOS Debug socket case reproduced a short receive while system-wide packet-drop counters surged under competing traffic. Quiet and focused repeats passed, so the correlation does not attribute the drops to RocketNet; a fix is not qualified." :cells (- n -))
    (:feature "The big-endian full-system run has no single all-green run yet: at 9232be69 the unit suite and the portable rung pass on s390x and the auto rung failed only test_server_port_zero_transport, whose compiled-out xdp refusal 8bbc8e41 now accepts (the case passes alone on the guest three of three); at af25b317 it passed alone three of three again. Known issue: one full-system guest run (unit, auto and portable rungs) of this head is still owed." :cells (n - -))
    (:feature "The full soak completed the portable, GSO, GSO-plain and io_uring 1000-client cells with non-timing PASS, then was killed during the AF_XDP cell. Cause: the fixed 16G virtme-ng guest is under the default profile's 16.96 GiB create-only plan, so the guest OOM-kills the load process (exit 137)." :cells (n - -) :note "rn-xdp-soak-cell: nightly-soak.yml sizes the xdp guest from LOAD_PLAN_ONLY=1 plus a measured run reserve, (plan + 1000 x 9848630 bytes) x 5/4 + 1 GiB (34G; the peak RSS is 1.54 x plan, 26.1 GiB in an unconstrained 48G guest at a40897f3), fails with a clear line when the runner's MemAvailable is short, and keeps the guest's exit, peak RSS and dmesg tail in vm.log. At c3409ab5 on a 121 GB fleet runner the xdp cell passed three runs in a row in the 34G guest (33.3 GiB MemTotal), peak RSS 26.1 GiB each (27397436-27398060 kB), wall 1:56-2:09, and the full many-client step passed all five cells in 485 s")
    (:feature "Windows manual Debug/toolchain/examples/soak/frame-budget coverage, and some macOS and Windows LAN rows were not completed before the release cut." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The 100-microsecond server-update p99 target is missed at larger client counts. Correctness passes are reported separately from timing failures." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Windows native-server LAN qualification awaits the replacement test NIC; existing Windows client evidence does not qualify the server path." :cells (- - n))
    (:feature "Live AF_XDP qualification used copy mode only. Zero-copy and line-rate performance are unqualified. io_uring suite-concurrency and runner memlock provisioning work is deferred." :cells (n - -))))
  (:id "known-issues"
   :title "Historical preview-1 known issues and plans"
   :text "Historical preview-1 planning retained for context. Some fixes listed here landed before preview-2, so this table does not state current preview-2 status; use the preview-2 known-issues table above."
   :label "known issue"
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Zero warnings at -Wconversion and the remaining strict flags, SDK and vendored libsodium (public header already clean at -Weverything)" :cells (n n n) :note "the default build is clean as errors on Linux (gcc, clang), macOS (Apple clang) and Windows (MSVC) at -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic and /W4; at -Wshadow -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wcast-qual -Wformat=2 -Wundef -Wdouble-promotion (ROCKETNET_STRICT_WARNINGS=ON) about 250 SDK and about 1000 vendored libsodium warnings remained until the wconv series and PR #454 (strict set on by default, as errors, on every compiler) landed on 2026-10-22, checked at the strict set on gcc 15, clang 21, Apple clang, MSVC and clang-cl before landing; the cells turn ✅ with green CI at a recorded head")
    (:feature "Client connect zeroes the client's 7.6 MB transport (about 3 ms) and disconnect wipes and frees it (about 1.6 ms). The final deliverable allocates the transport once at create, resets it in place on connect, and wipes only the secrets, by their size, on disconnect." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Claiming and releasing a server slot re-initialises its 1.48 MB region inside the update (0.11 to 0.36 ms each), and disconnecting all of 1000 clients takes about 20 ms, plus about 130 ms in the next update. The final deliverable resets only the state a slot used." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Large configurations still incur bulk memory wipes during shutdown. The 1000-client example soak can spike in memory and run out of memory on Linux. Secrets-only destroy is held for preview-3, not included in preview-2; completion polling does not remove the final synchronous cleanup cost." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The default configuration needs about 13.4 GB for a 1000-slot server, because each client's send reserve is sized for 10 Gbps for 2 seconds. The public light-client profile sizes a 1000-slot server at 955,710,336 bytes (955,710 bytes per slot) for 1000 players at 10 Hz and a client at 3,063,168 bytes." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The server decrypts and seals packets on the game thread; the client already decrypts on its I/O thread. The final deliverable moves server decrypt and seal off the game thread." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Native Linux server I/O uses bounded handoffs so the game thread does not wait on worker I/O or bulk copies. Messages and packets become visible after the worker completes the handoff, including on the following update. Exact-head p99 qualification remains pending." :cells (n - -) :note "the GSO, io_uring and XDP handoff implementations are landed at eaf420df45614fe1b0d8f1152b76b815d33cfdd2; the red cell records qualification, not missing implementation")
    (:feature "The portable server send and receive paths use bounded TX and RX workers instead of doing one game-thread system call per packet. Exact-head p99 qualification remains pending." :cells (n n n) :note "the portable TX and RX worker implementation is landed at eaf420df45614fe1b0d8f1152b76b815d33cfdd2; the red cells record qualification, not missing implementation")
    (:feature "One server update may process up to 16,000 received packets, each with its own decrypt, through three copies and extra keyed hashes per packet. The final deliverable bounds receive work per update by time as well as count, and removes the extra copies and hashes." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The acknowledgement statistics sweep scans thousands of records per update. The final deliverable keeps those statistics up to date as acks arrive." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Every main call is meant to take under 0.1 ms in Release under load; the server API p99 does not yet meet that budget at 1000 clients. The final deliverable measures every main call at 1000 clients on each platform and holds the result in a gate." :cells (n n n) :note "The coordinator reports approximately 2 ms at 1000 clients, but no final exact-head receipt is available in this checkout; the cells remain unqualified")
    (:feature "Each unreliable message is sent as its own packet; small unreliable messages are not packed together. The final deliverable packs small messages into shared packets and keeps in-place writes for large ones." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Client disconnect and server stop request shutdown without waiting for workers; client disconnected and server stopped check completion without joining or freeing. Both client and server transports follow stop, stopped, destroy. Destroy asserts completion and synchronously joins and frees; a stalled worker leaves completion false and storage alive. The implementation has landed; exact-head platform qualification remains pending." :cells (n n n) :note "the red cells record qualification, not missing API or lifecycle implementation")
    (:feature "On macOS, a portable-transport client connecting over IPv4 to a server that serves both IPv4 and IPv6 on one port failed to connect once, intermittently: observed once in a sharded functional run, not reproduced on rerun, and test_transport_dual_stack_ipv4_client passed in the full run at b0a8a2e3. The final deliverable finds the cause and proves every family combination on macOS by repeated functional runs." :cells (- n -))
    (:feature "On macOS, the historical full functional suite ran past CI's 120-second limit; it passed outside CI (all 142 cases at b0a8a2e3, about 6 m 38 s). The macOS CI restructuring is held for preview-3; preview-2 qualification depends on its own exact-head receipts." :cells (- n -))
    (:feature "Some functional tests measure operating-system behaviour rather than RocketNet: test_macos_client_timing_default_qos, test_macos_client_timing_taskpolicy_background, the test_thread_priority_timing cases and test_thread_priority_windows_readback. The final deliverable removes them or rewrites them to test only RocketNet's own code." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The macOS client timing functional test carries a branch that lowers the game thread's priority, which no case uses since its last caller was removed. The final deliverable removes the branch with the cases above." :cells (- n -))
    (:feature "The Windows Debug, AddressSanitizer and Application Verifier runs passed before the last v1.0.0-preview-1 API changes and have not been repeated on the released API. The final deliverable repeats all three on the released API, on every Windows transport." :cells (- - n))
    (:feature "Client connect and server start still allocate: the client's transport, socket and I/O thread at each connect, and the server's transport and its tables at each start. The final deliverable builds them at create, so nothing allocates after create." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "A few allocations do not go through the caller's allocator: AF_XDP packet memory, io_uring rings, the RIO registered region, thread stacks, interface discovery and the C library's output buffer. The final deliverable routes them through the caller's allocator where the operating system allows, and reports the rest by size." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The memory plan reports what create needs, but not yet what connect, reconnect, start and stop need. The final deliverable extends the plan to the whole session, so one block sized from the plan alone never runs out." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The handshake's signature-failure budget is kept per address and port, so one host rotating its ports can force up to 1024 signature checks per update. The final deliverable keys the budget by host address and caps signature checks per update." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Connect-token claims are first come, first served, so an observer on the network path can copy a client's first request and hold its token until the handshake deadline. The final deliverable's security pass closes this window or bounds it and documents it." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "A replayed connection response refreshes a slot's receive time, a token claim is not released on three refusal paths, and a forged cookie can rewind a client's handshake (bounded). The final deliverable fixes each one, with a test for each." :cells (n n n) :note "the future-token part is tracked separately: PR #433 introduced the refusal and deleted the lifetime cap; preview-3 raises the server's explicit clock-skew allowance from five seconds to 30 seconds")
    (:feature "At very low send rates, time spent waiting for send budget counts toward the reliable-message timeout. The final deliverable counts only the time a message has been on the wire." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Sequenced blocks and small records treat an in-turn record differently. The final deliverable gives both one rule, modelled and tested." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Ack processing costs O(k²) per block, and the packet builder O(items²) per class pass. The final deliverable makes both linear." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The example soak can fail when many clients disconnect at once: the server still counts connected clients after the disconnect pass. The final deliverable fixes the disconnect path and runs the example soak green on every platform." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The full client I/O TLA+ model needs a configuration that fits the CI time budget. The final deliverable splits it into configurations that each finish within the budget." :cells (n - -))
    (:feature "The reconnect churn and UDP loopback functional cases showed rare timing failures under heavy machine load. The final deliverable makes them independent of machine load." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The receipt read returns how many outcomes it copied, not how many there were when the caller's buffer is too short (ring overflow is counted, in receipts_dropped). The final deliverable returns the available count." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Connect over whichever family works: send connection requests to the token's IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and keep the first that answers (TLA+ first)." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Backend keygen, connect-token minting and a reference server registration in Go and C#." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The v1.0.0-preview-1 API is provisional: names, structure and doc comments in the public header may still change. The final deliverable finalizes the API after customer feedback." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The receive path still accepts a datagram up to 1472 bytes (a 1439-byte payload), above the 1416-byte ROCKETNET_MAX_PACKET_PAYLOAD_BYTES every sender writes; the standard test vectors depend on the larger bound. The final deliverable refuses anything above the send bound and regenerates the vectors." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The config field max_payload_bytes bounds the largest message, but max_message_bytes is already the name of a different field, so the rename to the message name waits. The final deliverable gives each of the two fields a name that says which limit it is." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Internal identifiers still use the old payload, ring, slot and window names that the public header no longer uses. The final deliverable renames them to the public terms in one pass." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The two config fields max_payload_bytes (the largest payload the transport fragments) and max_message_bytes (the largest message) are still separate; the final deliverable merges them into one max_message_bytes with one maximum, ROCKETNET_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES, and states the max_payload_bytes limit through a define rather than the literal 305408." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The client and the server measure packet_loss and jitter differently: the client measures loss of the server packets it receives and the change in arrival gaps, the server measures unacknowledged sends and round-trip spread. The final deliverable gives each stat one definition on both ends." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The development network simulator takes effect on a client connection at the next connect, and on a server at the next start, unless that connection already runs a simulator; the final deliverable applies it at once on a live connection too." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The internal headers have no extern \"C\" blocks, so a C tool cannot include them. The final deliverable adds them where a C caller needs one." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Client connect from a handshake or token failure state (CONNECTION_DENIED .. CONNECT_TOKEN_EXPIRED) is refused until rocketnet_client_disconnect; the final deliverable lets connect start over from any failure state (TLA+ first)." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The *_name lookups return two forms: status names are the enum suffix (\"OK\") and the client state, log level and disconnect reason names are lower-case words. The final deliverable returns the upper-case enum suffix from all four." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "A Linux build with XDP off still needs the BPF and XDP development libraries. The final deliverable makes them optional when XDP is off." :cells (n - -))
    (:feature "The public header carries a large volume of comments, some citing internal design references; the examples are longer than they need to be; the build has many targets. The final deliverable states each rule once in the header, shortens the examples and trims the build targets." :cells (n - -))))
  (:id "final-deliverable"
   :title "Final deliverable: hardening and long testing"
   :text "Soaks, load, stress, transport matrices, fuzzing, sanitizers, nightlies and the TLA+ ledger, run for the final deliverable after v1.0.0-preview-1. Every row here is planned for the final deliverable."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "A thousand clients for ten minutes on every transport of every platform, over the LAN, every guarantee checked" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Linux: every transport cell fifty times in a row with zero flakes, and the functional suite under ASan per transport" :cells (n - -) :note "docs/runs/linux-transport-cells-50x.md at ac4206a69acd83840c27d2ea024f6cc3712d734f records fifty runs per socket cell (portable, gso and io_uring pairings and loopback) with zero failures and one ASan pass per cell, the xdp cell not made there; docs/runs/gso-asan-connect-cycle-stall.md at b159a67c records forty reruns of the one ASan stall case with zero stalls. Cited as delivery records, this final-deliverable row stays not-done until its own qualification")
    (:feature "macOS: every transport cell fifty times in a row, zero flakes, nightly" :cells (- n -) :note "docs/runs/macos-transport-cells-50x.md at 13b7b291 records fifty runs per cell (portable, msgx and loopback pairings, 1000 runs) with zero failures over loopback; cited as a delivery record, this row stays not-done until its own nightly qualification")
    (:feature "A thousand clients against a Windows server, on every Windows transport" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Windows soaks per transport under loss, jitter and duplication, with flat handles and memory" :cells (- - n) :note "docs/runs/windows-soak-native-server.md at 3f900fa1254d938e50150bcb3386a5a0bb857e1a (1800 seconds per cell, iocp and rio) and docs/runs/windows-soak-portable.md at 74b8bb7f (1800 seconds, portable) record same-host loopback soaks under impairment with flat resources, each PASS; cited as delivery records, this row stays not-done until its own qualification")
    (:feature "Every Windows transport, every address family, fifty times clean" :cells (- - n) :note "docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x.md at b225201d4954a116e861d992516501ada88e5078 (70 seconds, portable and loopback cells) and docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x-native.md at 689f0947 (iocp and rio cells) each record fifty runs per cell with zero failures over loopback; cited as delivery records, this row stays not-done until its own qualification")
    (:feature "Linux: thirty-minute soaks per transport under impairment with flat fds, threads and memory" :cells (n - -) :note "docs/runs/linux-soak-30min-per-transport.md at adca4345bf963c7bcb5396ce5cd80a5111793533 records 1800 seconds per cell (portable, gso, gso-plain, io_uring and xdp) under impairment with flat resources, every cell PASS, and docs/runs/linux-soak-impaired-xdp-loss.md analyses the xdp cell server-to-client loss at the same 1800-second scope; cited as delivery records, this final-deliverable row stays not-done until its own qualification run")
    (:feature "Linux: 1000 light clients on every transport" :cells (n - -) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Linux: a hard-killed client or an ICMP error never stalls portable, gso, io_uring or xdp" :cells (n - -) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "macOS: 1000 clients per transport, three runs each, with the fd limit and counts in the summary" :cells (- n -) :note "docs/runs/lan-1000-proof.md records one macOS msgx run of 1000 clients for 600 seconds at 813b4adbe3dec2eee496577e3da2c0d7d66b8063; three runs per transport are not recorded, so this row stays not-done")
    (:feature "macOS: ASan, UBSan and TSan with Apple clang, and the leaks tool, on every suite and transport, nightly" :cells (- n -) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Linux: the nightly soak jobs green at the branch" :cells (n - -) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "The fuzz targets build and run under libFuzzer on Windows" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Create, destroy, connect, restart: a thousand times on Windows with nothing left behind" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Windows nightlies: all jobs run, warnings gated, verifier script safe" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "TLA ledger: every case finishes or says why; docs current" :cells (y - -) :evidence ((Linux "Runtime source a76d641a has the same TLA tree as qualified b4c0a109: all 287 required cases across 44 groups passed with unchanged input hashes, no missing configurations and clean stale and ledger-merge checks. Eighteen of 21 separate bench cases retain explicit bounded-timeout results and are not counted as passes")))
    (:feature "Server send capacity is sized from the config, never a fixed 256" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "macOS: 1000 light clients on msgx and portable" :cells (- n -) :note "docs/runs/macos-soak-per-transport.md at 31ad78624a5d46f873678ecaaeb884bdbe1af72f records 1800-second msgx and portable soaks, not a 1000-light-client run; this row stays not-done")
    (:feature "Windows: 1000 light clients on portable, iocp and rio" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "macOS: the nightly soak job green at the branch" :cells (- n -) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Ack receipts: LOSS only after the receipt deadline" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "The whole tree formatted with clang-format in the netcode style, the format checked in CI" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")))
  (:id "final-contraction"
   :title "Final contraction pass"
   :text "The last pass before v1.0.0: the library shrunk to the size and readability of netcode and yojimbo, one layer at a time from the bottom, with no change a caller can see. The public API, the wire format and every guarantee stay as they are; the existing unit, functional and soak suites and the TLA+ models guard each layer while it shrinks."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Each layer's job written in one sentence, and the list corrected by the owner before any code changes" :cells (n - -) :note "owner, 2026-10-28: \"This is the final contraction pass.\" Start from the seven layers in CLAUDE.md, including any that exist only as scattered code")
    (:feature "Layer 1, init, allocator, logging and assertions: contracted" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Layer 2, leaf utilities (address, hash, base64, bounded containers): contracted" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Layer 3, platform (threads, mutexes, clocks, sockets): contracted, with far fewer preprocessor branches" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable; sdk/rocketnet_platform.cpp is 6,568 lines with 108 conditional blocks at f981340d")
    (:feature "Layer 4, transport protocol (token, cookie, handshake, keys, replay, acks, packets): contracted" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Layer 5, message layer (reliability, ordering, fragmentation, receipts, receive queue): contracted" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Layer 6, runtime transports: there is no driver; a driver is the transport. The sdk/rocketnet_driver* files and names are folded into the transports, each as small as its platform allows" :cells (n n n) :note "owner, 2026-10-28: \"I cut the concept of driver. A driver *is* the transport. There should be no driver.\" Six sdk/rocketnet_driver* files remain at f981340d")
    (:feature "Layer 7, public C API: contracted, with no change to rocketnet.h behaviour" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Comments say what the code does, not why a review was satisfied" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Tests and tools contracted alongside: library tests out of sdk/, unit cases run in layer order from layer 1 up, no case kept only for a deleted mechanism" :cells (n n n) :note "owner, 2026-10-28: \"this layer set, is the order that your unit tests should test things in too\"; sdk/rocketnet_tests.cpp is 16,426 lines at f981340d")
    (:feature "The library is readable end to end in an afternoon: sdk/ total recorded before and after" :cells (n n n) :note "sdk/ is 98,906 lines at f981340d")))
  (:id "release"
   :title "Release and process"
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Release hardening flags" :cells (n n n) :note "fe7966f adds tools/check_hardening.py; no workflow runs it, so no platform has a run")
    (:feature "Reproducible vendored sources" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: ci.yml reproduces the committed sodium pair on the Linux runners; 23d4c40 sodium; f6457b5 XDP archive" :note "reproducible release dependencies as a whole are still owed")
    (:feature "An integrating application vendors the SDK and proves it (release gate)" :cells (n n n) :note "held. The ultimate soak: vendored byte for byte, the server runs under real conditions. The application loop pegs to real time with drop-frame detection, so update stays non-blocking with time passed in and bounded walks, and nothing in the transports blocks or takes unbounded time in update")
    (:feature "Supported-platform policy" :cells (n - -) :note "34406ce docs/PLATFORMS.md; 1952f918 wires tools/check_platform_policy.py in .github/workflows/ci.yml:427; tools/check_platform_policy.py exits 0 (4 supported, 9 nightly, 3 unsupported rows match); a passing CI run is owed")
    (:feature "v1.0.0-preview-3 release candidate: shipping label, release notes and qualification record" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: native Release unit and functional suites passed at 126ef062 with zero warnings in both builds; docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md, docs/RELEASE-NOTES-v1.0.0-preview-3.md" :note "the tag waits for the owner's review of sdk/rocketnet.h and the space vendor and soak gates at tag time")
    (:feature "Security disclosure and release process" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; 6795ac1 SECURITY.md, docs/RELEASING.md" :note "tools/check_release_doc.py passes by hand; no workflow runs it")
    (:feature "Independent review of the connection layer repair diff, received" :cells (n - -) :note "the repair of findings #143 to #159; a review request sent is not a review received or an approval")))))
